<article class="env-lemma" id="0DM2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DM2">Lemma <span data-tag="0DM2">108.5.1</span>.</a> The diagonal of $\mathrm{Quot}_{\mathcal{F}/X/B} \to B$ is a closed immersion. If $\mathcal{F}$ is of finite type, then the diagonal is a closed immersion of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose we have a scheme $T/B$ and two quotients $\mathcal{F}_ T \to \mathcal{Q}_ i$, $i = 1, 2$ corresponding to $T$-valued points of $\mathrm{Quot}_{\mathcal{F}/X/B}$ over $B$. Denote $\mathcal{K}_1$ the kernel of the first one and set $u : \mathcal{K}_1 \to \mathcal{Q}_2$ the composition. By Flatness on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/083M" data-tag="083M">77.8.6</a> there is a closed subspace of $T$ such that $T' \to T$ factors through it if and only if the pullback $u_{T'}$ is zero. This proves the diagonal is a closed immersion. Moreover, if $\mathcal{F}$ is of finite type, then $\mathcal{K}_1$ is of finite type (Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/082T" data-tag="082T">18.24.2</a>) and we see that the diagonal is of finite presentation by the same lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>